  "data": {
    "body": "Determine which of the following statements are true and which are false.\n\nI. The series $\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty \\frac{1}{k^4+1}$ is convergent by the limit comparison test with $\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty \\frac{1}{k^4}$. \n\nII. The series $\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty \\frac{1}{k^4+1}$ is convergent by the comparison test with $\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty \\frac{1}{k^4}$. \n\nIII. The series $\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty \\frac{1}{k^4+1}$ is convergent by the ratio test. ",
    "solution": [
